  (polyline (pts (xy 20.32 184.15) (xy 191.77 184.15) (xy 191.77 260.35) (xy 20.32 260.35) (xy 20.32 184.15))
    (stroke (width 0.254) (type default))
    (uuid 030bdc73-d67d-5e19-a96e-625ac0666cea)
  )
  (text "NOTES" (at 22.86 190.5 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 7d2e1eb6-2bd2-5a80-aee0-7771178bda3b)
  )
  (text "1.  There is no PCB. This is a point-to-point (flying-lead) build: wire by SIGNAL NAME, not by\n    connector pin number. DS1's pin order varies between vendors -- check it against the silkscreen\n    on your module before cutting wire.\n\n2.  Every pin assignment here is duplicated in include/board_config.h and in the -D TFT_* build flags\n    in platformio.ini. All three must agree; CI checks this on every push.\n\n3.  A1's on-board charger runs BT1 whenever USB-C is connected. It has NO load disconnect, so the\n    low-voltage cutoff is done in firmware (VBAT_CUTOFF_VOLTS, 3.20 V, then deep sleep).\n\n4.  R3 is not fitted by default. Fit it only if the backlight glows faintly during deep sleep: GPIO21\n    is not an RTC GPIO, so it cannot be held low and goes high-impedance once A1 sleeps.\n\n5.  GPIO2 (D0) is a strapping pin that must be high at boot. R1/R2 hold it near 2.1 V with a charged\n    cell, which reads as high, so the divider is safe. If R1/R2 are omitted, set VBAT_SENSE_FITTED =\n    false in board_config.h -- otherwise the floating pin reads as a flat cell.\n\n6.  GPIO21 (D6) is also UART0 TX. The ROM bootloader toggles it, so the backlight flickers for about\n    200 ms at power-on. Cosmetic only.\n\n7.  D4/GPIO6 and D5/GPIO7 are left free as an I2C pair for a future sensor (see the roadmap in\n    README.md). D9/GPIO9 is a boot-mode strapping pin and is deliberately left unconnected.\n\n8.  SPI runs at 40 MHz, which is only reliable over short leads. Keep SCK and MOSI short, twist them\n    with a ground return, and drop SPI_FREQUENCY to 27 MHz or 20 MHz if the panel shows noise.\n\n9.  DS1's MISO is unused and left unconnected (TFT_MISO = -1). The panel is never read back.\n\n10.  Assembly: strain-relieve the display flex, and keep BT1 out of the crown of the hat where it can\n    be squashed or punctured." (at 22.86 194.31 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 644cbaf4-a889-5a49-b5ef-c842840b8420)
  )
